        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "ac6397e156f9b2d343e37988d930d5b689a0cc7eeeb220c72803797519b55dea"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This has a solution of $$ u(p)=\\frac{\\int_{0}^{p}G(x)dx}{\\int_{0}^{1}G(x)dx} $$ where $ G(x) $ is defined by Equation A1.12 (Kimura 1962). More generally, for any diffusion (regardless of the nature of the boundaries), the probability that the process reaches a value of b before a value of a, given it starts at p (where $ A < a < p < b < B $, with the diffusion defined over $ A < x < B $), is $$ u_{b,a}(p)=\\frac{\\int_{a}^{p}G(x)dx}{\\int_{a}^{b}G(x)dx} $$",
      "source_page": 1178,
      "source_pages": [
        1178
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
